$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl Anilines. A mixture of
N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the corresponding boronic
acid (1.6 equiv), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and
potassium carbonate (2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was
stirred at 80 °C under an argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction
mixture was diluted with AcOEt, washed with water and brine, dried over
MgSO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified
by column chromatography (hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product.
tert-Butyl
3-(2-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)phenyl)-1H-pyrrole-1-carboxylate. The
product was obtained following the general procedure (1.8 mmol scale) as
pale yellow solids (606 mg, 94%) after purification by column
chromatography. mp 94-98 °C (hexanes/ EtOAc); Rf = 0.32 (10%
AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 8.05 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.39-7.31 (m,
2H), 7.31-7.23 (m, 2H), 7.05 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 6.77 (br s,
1H), 6.36 (dd, J = 3.2 Hz, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 1.62 (s, 9H), 1.50 (s, 9H); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ 152.9, 148.5, 135.6, 129.6, 128.0, 124.5, 124.0, 123.0,
121.0, 119.8, 118.1, 112.6, 84.1, 80.3, 28.3, 28.0; IR (KBr) νmax 3414,
2326, 1744, 1721, 1585, 1512, 1485, 1447, 1381, 1346 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z
358 (M+), 303 (M -t-Bu + 2H), 246 (M -2t-Bu + 2H); HRMS-ESI (m/z) calcd
for C20H27N2O4 [M + H]+ 359.1965, found 359.1954. Anal. Calcd for
C20H26N2O4: C, 67.02; H, 7.31; N, 7.82. Found: C, 66.84; H, 7.39; N,
7.78.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development of a Bronsted Acid-Promoted Arene-Ynamide Cyclization toward
