$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (i) A sealable vial was charged with 5-chloro-2,3-difluoropyridine (1.01
g, 6.76 mmol), X-Phos (0.32 g, 0.68 mmol), palladium(II) acetate (76 mg,
0.34 mmol), potassium phosphate (4.31 g, 20.3 mmol), and phenylboronic
acid (1.00 g, 8.11 mmol). The vial was sealed, and dioxane (27 mL) was
added. The mixture was degassed by bubbling with N2 and then heated at
100 °C for 30 min. The mixture was concentrated and purified by MPLC
using a gradient of 0-40% EtOAc in hexanes. 2,3-difluoro-5-phenylpyridine
(1.21 g, 6.33 mmol, 94% yield) as a white solid.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
